00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.310 align:start position:0%
 
phenotracker is a deep phenotyping  platform that helps generate continuous  high throughput data  to characterize disease and intervention  in the next few minutes i will share  with you  what the platform does why it was  developed where we are in its  development and what it can achieve for  drug testing and repurposing  disease in humans is well characterized  mainly because doctors are continuously  monitoring patients  such data allows us to see variability  in disease stages levels of severity  understand how these influence outcomes  and study treatment responses  such detailed clinical information has  led to a paradigm shift in medical  practice  and clinical trials stratification of  patients  personalized medical treatment and  precision molecular diagnostics that  accompany treatment selection  animal models on the other hand which  are critical to advance  compounds into clinical use often do not  reproduce accurately such detail  for example animal models and experiment  factors are typically selected  for lethal endpoints rather than  examining natural variability in stages  of disease progression that are observed  in humans  natural manifestation of disease in  small animals is not well defined  and many questions that would be  important for treatment  go on unexplored leading to course  observations at the same time close to  40  percent of candidate compounds failed to  become drugs in part due to the  bottleneck of preclinical development  during this stage researchers study  compounds that show efficacy in cell  lines or organoids  to understand efficacy and toxicity at  the biological system level  which has complex metabolism immune  responses and  tolerance for both disease and treatment  interestingly  over 60 percent of animal models used  for such  testing are mice rats or other animals  such as  hamsters or ferrets to address the  challenge  of detailed disease monitoring and  quantification of drug responses in  pre-clinical animal testing  we developed a platform for deep  phenotyping  and deep learning it is an alternative  to an  all-present doctor that sees each animal  individually 24 7. importantly  such high throughput data acquisition  from animal experiments  often fails due to instrument complexity  and high costs resulting in short-term  observation studies  with limited sensitivity to account for  long-term trends in animal condition  physiology  without significant invasiveness that's  why the system that we built  is a balance between ease of use cost  effectiveness  scalability and long-term monitoring  capabilities  phenotracker is a tracking and analysis  platform  that is designed to collect continuous  data from multiple  sensors and extract characteristics of  animal physiology  body vitals behavior and even the  underlying  state the animal is in powered by deep  learning  the system provides real-time alerts  extracts  meaningful trends and data and brings  the lab experiment within reach  for researchers that are not present or  not able to be in the lab  when the animal is showing important  changes associated with the studied  condition  that's why the way the system works is a  combination  of hardware optimization and software  designed to reveal important information  that is not obvious from  short-term observation real-time raw  data using thermal and infrared sensors  are captured and sent to the cloud for  processing  there each animal is analyzed for  posture changes  speed of movement and other features  including  advanced seasonality decomposition and  deep learning  here on the left you can see the  captured information  after body detection and on the right we  show how  each 10-minute interval of video is  analyzed to reveal patterns  using multiple data points ultimately  these vary significantly between  pre-infection  and post-infection conditions something  that might be easily missed  if you were to look at the cage for just  a few minutes  once the data is acquired from a sensor  it is separated into individual features  normalized and prepared for comparison  from user-generated metadata  to capture changes in amplitude and  periodicity  we separate the trends into individual  segments which are compared to the  baseline  of the individual animal during the  healthy stage before the  start of the experiment then data is  analyzed for variation from baseline and  used to train a predictive machine  learning model  that incorporates system dynamics into  its prediction of outcomes  on top of this process we developed a  software layer to provide real-time view  of raw video stream  process data as well as custom alerts  for anomalies and state changes to help  incorporate such insights  into experiment design and intervention  additional tools for big data analysis  allow the user to compare and contrast  the data from a given experiment  to accumulated data sets in our  proprietary database  of animal phenotypic patterns the  interface helps bring  the experiment to the user making it  possible to view  explore and run big data analysis  interactively in the cloud as well as  explore the results of this analysis  in comparison to ongoing experiments  that are being conducted  as a result this proprietary high  throughput data can be used  to train a predictive model of animal  disease progression  that allows a detailed analysis of  phenotypic and molecular data  to extract biomarkers associated with  pathogen type  stage of disease progression treatment  response  recovery rate and even population  dynamics of animal to animal interaction  or disease spread continuously  monitoring these conditions  and changes for each stage animal  and organ molecular profiles using  rna-seq  can show how the body reacts to  infection what types of pathways are  activated  and how this can be used to describe the  biology of infection  that drives disease progression our team  has been working on several different  prototypes  viruses vaccines and treatments working  with labs  at university of california san  francisco  tulane university and louisiana state  university  we tested and refined the hardware for  use in biosafety level 2  and biosafety level 3 facilities develop  solutions for different animal models  designed and tested our software with  lab technicians and research users  and as a result we have collected data  on enteroviruses  covid19 compared routes of infection and  now  we are testing interventions for  efficacy and toxicity  in the next six months we plan to a  complete ongoing experiments and publish  findings with our research collaborators  b develop several more cages based on  demand from partner labs  and test new sensors for specialized  experiments  c ultimately we plan to demonstrate how  this type of data can be utilized for  basic research  drug testing as well as characterization  of treatment response to optimize  and shorten preclinical testing in  reality there are so many unknowns about  disease and animal models  and if we are to use animals responsibly  and understand how these biological  systems can mimic  human disease and help us develop novel  interventions  we have to develop a model of  personalized disease dynamics  high throughput data and precise  understanding of how disease  develops will ultimately open the door  for new treatments  new knowledge new capabilities our goal  is to make this platform a standard part  of all  animal experiments and a major component  of animal testing  together with our collaborators we are  working on a number of high impact  projects that include source code two  treatment testing  a variety of vaccines as well as  experiments that can help  optimize intervention timing and prevent  transmission  we believe that this technology is a  powerful platform for pharmaceutical  model of drug discovery  testing and drug repurposing with so  many companies turning to ai  guided drug design analytical drug  repurposing models and discovery of  novel  compounds phenotracker is a competitive  advantage  in the hands of experts with insights  into animal condition  testing strategies collected baseline  data  as well as the capability to help design  novel sensors that provide  unique insights into the many aspects of  health  and disease thank you for taking the  time to learn about phenotracker  the studies i described today were done  in collaboration with ucsf  tulane and lsu and we're funded by darpa  nih and nsf grants for any additional  questions  feel free to reach out to me elia  pine.bio  or visit our website fino.tracker.com

